Check that /novcautodetect is accepted and changes nothing: lld-link does not
search for Visual Studio by default, while explicit /winsysroot, /vctoolsdir
and /libpath keep working. The default and /vcautodetect are in vcautodetect.test.

# RUN: rm -rf %t.dir && mkdir -p %t.dir/sysroot/VC/Tools/MSVC/1.1.1.1/lib/x64
# RUN: cp %p/Inputs/std64.lib %t.dir/sysroot/VC/Tools/MSVC/1.1.1.1/lib/x64

Explicit /winsysroot is still honored.
# RUN: lld-link %p/Inputs/hello64.obj /novcautodetect /winsysroot:%t.dir/sysroot \
# RUN:   /defaultlib:std64 /entry:main /out:%t.exe /verbose 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck --check-prefix=FOUND %s

Explicit /vctoolsdir is still honored.
# RUN: lld-link %p/Inputs/hello64.obj /novcautodetect \
# RUN:   /vctoolsdir:%t.dir/sysroot/VC/Tools/MSVC/1.1.1.1 \
# RUN:   /defaultlib:std64 /entry:main /out:%t.exe /verbose 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck --check-prefix=FOUND %s

FOUND: VC toolchain: {{.*}}sysroot{{[/\\]}}VC{{[/\\]}}Tools{{[/\\]}}MSVC{{[/\\]}}1.1.1.1

With /novcautodetect the environment is not consulted, and no VC toolchain or
SDK path is detected at all.
# RUN: env -u LIB VCToolsInstallDir=%t.dir/sysroot/VC/Tools/MSVC/1.1.1.1 \
# RUN:   not lld-link %p/Inputs/hello64.obj /novcautodetect /defaultlib:std64 \
# RUN:   /entry:main /out:%t.exe /verbose 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck --check-prefix=NONE --implicit-check-not="VC toolchain:" \
# RUN:     --implicit-check-not="SDK lib path:" \
# RUN:     --implicit-check-not="UCRT lib path:" %s

NONE: LINK : fatal error LNK1181: input file 'std64.lib' was not found

/libpath still works with /novcautodetect.
# RUN: lld-link %p/Inputs/hello64.obj /novcautodetect \
# RUN:   /libpath:%t.dir/sysroot/VC/Tools/MSVC/1.1.1.1/lib/x64 \
# RUN:   /defaultlib:std64 /entry:main /out:%t.exe

/winsdkdir alone adds the Windows SDK lib path with no VC toolchain, and std64.lib
is found there. (Verbose lines are only printed on a successful link here.)
# RUN: mkdir -p %t.dir/sdk/Include/10.0.1.1 %t.dir/sdk/Lib/10.0.1.1/um/x64
# RUN: cp %p/Inputs/std64.lib %t.dir/sdk/Lib/10.0.1.1/um/x64
# RUN: env -u LIB lld-link %p/Inputs/hello64.obj /winsdkdir:%t.dir/sdk \
# RUN:   /defaultlib:std64 /entry:main /out:%t.exe /verbose 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck --check-prefix=SDK --implicit-check-not="VC toolchain:" %s

SDK: Windows SDK lib path: {{.*}}sdk{{[/\\]}}Lib{{[/\\]}}10.0.1.1{{[/\\]}}um

With /winsdkdir alone and LIB set, LIB is ignored and the user is told why. (The
link succeeds from the SDK dir: lit's LLD_IN_TEST drops buffered warnings on a
fatal exit, so the warning is checked on a successful link.)
# RUN: env LIB=%t.dir/sysroot/VC/Tools/MSVC/1.1.1.1/lib/x64 \
# RUN:   lld-link %p/Inputs/hello64.obj /winsdkdir:%t.dir/sdk \
# RUN:   /defaultlib:std64 /entry:main /out:%t.exe > %t.warn.txt 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck --check-prefix=WARN %s < %t.warn.txt

WARN: warning: ignoring %LIB%: no VC toolchain was resolved

/vctoolsversion alone resolves no toolchain and does not suppress LIB.
# RUN: env LIB=%t.dir/sysroot/VC/Tools/MSVC/1.1.1.1/lib/x64 \
# RUN:   lld-link %p/Inputs/hello64.obj /vctoolsversion:1.1.1.1 \
# RUN:   /defaultlib:std64 /entry:main /out:%t.exe
